That said, you should ascend that in about 50k turns from where you
are.

#1 hint to decrease turns: don't altar camp or anything else where you
basically stand around doing nothing (pudding farming, etc).  I mean,
emptying out wands/scrolls of create monster at an altar is fine, but
no standing around hoping for golden glows and such.  It's a waste of
time anyway, except for extreme conducts, and you really only need 1
halfway decent weapon.

#2 Learn to use /teleport and jumping (save and bless your !speed so
you are still very fast) to cross Astral (and use conflict on
Astral/Air/Fire), and save your !FullHealing instead of quaffing them
immediately so that you have them to heal you _and_ add 8HP instead of
the latter.  Having AC-30 with 250HP is plenty of overkill for the
endgame, once you are a bit familiar with it.  And once you know that,
you can stop wasting time overpreparing down to AC-45 and 400+ HP.

#3 learn to levelport.  Tin up tengu to get telecontrol, once you have
it use cursed ?teleport to go to/from your stash.

#4 don't be obsessive about mapping all of Gehennom.  That was my big
problem. Use magic mapping/clairvoyance (the latter can be purchased
from the Valley priest) and just run through gehennom locating all the
staircases.  Yeah, you're missing a bit of loot there.  But you
probably don't need it anyway.  Demon mapping works too, or the Eyes.

#5 You don't have to kill everything.  Running past it is fine.



